# Config options for the spi_flash_id sample application

# Copyright (c) 2026 AgRV Contributors
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

mainmenu "AgRV2K SPI flash bring-up"

config APP_SPI_LONG_XFER
	bool "Also run the long (>4 byte) transfers through the engine's DMA path"
	default y
	help
	  Read the flash's 64-bit unique ID (0x4B + four dummy bytes + eight ID
	  bytes) twice and require the same answer: the reply is longer than the
	  phase data register, so the driver drains it with RX DMA.

	  Then probe the transmit side with a padded Write-Enable: 32 bytes
	  (eight register-fed phases) and 36 bytes (past them, so the driver
	  hands phase1 to the DMAC). Those two printouts are informational —
	  this part leaves WEL clear when 0x06 is followed by filler bytes — the
	  sample README explains what the verdict actually is.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
